      "message": "Hi Dave,\n\nAdding you as a reviewer. This is a small fix for mss_clamp: the plugin\nkeeps per-interface state after the interface is deleted, so a new\ninterface that reuses the sw_if_index looks clamped but isn\u0027t, and\nre-enabling with the same parameters is a no-op.\n\nI ran into this when re-creating GRE tunnels in VPP: the new tunnels got\nthe sw_if_index of the deleted ones and silently lost MSS clamping, so\nTCP SYNs went through with MSS 1460 over a 1476-byte tunnel MTU. The\nonly workaround was ip4 disable/enable on the affected interfaces.\n\nCI is green. Once it\u0027s merged, would it be possible to cherry-pick it\nto stable/2610 and stable/2606?\n\nThanks!",
